steps.text:
Cardiac output has to serve working muscle *and* skin. In the heat three things squeeze it:

- blood sent to warm skin is blood not sent to muscle, and some of it pools in skin veins, so less returns to fill the heart;
- sweat loss shrinks plasma volume, filling the heart less again [[c:cs-dehydration-strain]];
- heat and hot skin lower **VO₂max** [[c:cs-vo2max-drop]].

The last point is easy to miss. If VO₂max falls, the same 250 W becomes a higher percentage of it. The effort is relatively harder, heart rate and perceived effort climb, and you tire sooner or slow down.
